        <h1 class="subpage-subhero-content-heading" data-ix="slide-in-bottom-2-delay">Modern Cold Therapy Has Been Used To Relieve Pain For Over 150 Years!</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="subpage-subhero-content-right">
        <p class="paragraph" data-ix="slide-in-bottom-3-delay">It goes back to James Arnott MD, the pioneer of cryotherapy. He used a mixture of ice and salt to treat headaches in 1849. Ancient manuscripts even show cold water was used for the same purpose by the Ancient Egyptians.</p>
        <p class="paragraph" data-ix="slide-in-bottom-3-delay">Scientific studies show cold therapy soothes your head pain. The many studies you’re about to read will shock you (who knew ice worked so well?) and make you wonder why more people don’t use cold therapy.</p>
        <p class="paragraph last-paragraph" data-ix="slide-in-bottom-3-delay">In short: The cold “overrides” your pain signals. Instead of feeling pain you just feel the cold.</p>
